# ==============================================================================
# tools/libgit2-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# THE FIRST RULE BELOW ("!*") IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores names that also occur inside the vendored libgit2 and Mbed TLS
# trees and in this folder's own scripts, for example:
#
#     *.env                     -> linux/pins.env
#     [Dd]ebug/  [Rr]elease/  [Oo]ut/  [Ll]og/  bld/  [Oo]bj/ ...
#     [Aa][Rr][Mm]64/  *.obj  *.pdb  ...
#
# Without the "!*" below, such files would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the vendored snapshots (or the build pins) would not be there
# for the next person who cloned this repository. A nested .gitignore takes
# precedence over the ones above it, so re-including everything here and then
# re-ignoring only what this folder genuinely produces is the correct fix - and
# it keeps the root .gitignore untouched. (Same rule, same reason, as
# CodeBrix.Sdl3's sdl3-native-tools/.gitignore.)
#
# libgit2/.gitignore, libgit2/tests/resources/**/.gitignore and
# mbedtls/**/.gitignore are UPSTREAM's own files and part of the unmodified
# snapshots. They are deeper than this one, so they still apply inside their
# trees - which is correct: they only name build products, and for both
# pinned commits `git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard` upstream lists NOTHING,
# so no upstream-tracked file is hidden by them (see ../UPSTREAM.txt).
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git status --ignored --porcelain -- tools/libgit2-native-tools
#         -> should list only output/ contents (and nothing at all on a clean
#            clone)
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built native libraries, unstripped copies, smoke-test binaries, SHA256SUMS,
# build scratch. ONE tree, shared by every platform build.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH MATTERS: without it the pattern would match ANY directory
# named "output" at any depth, including inside the vendored trees.
# NOTE THE TRAILING /* RATHER THAN A BARE /output/: a directory that is itself
# excluded is never descended into, so the "!" rule below could never
# re-include the README inside it.
/output/*

# ...except the placeholder README that explains what goes there.
!/output/README.txt

# Python's bytecode cache, written next to android/verify.py whenever
# android/build.py imports it.
__pycache__/

# Finder droppings. Needed explicitly: the "!*" above re-includes everything
# under this folder and so overrides any .DS_Store rule inherited from the root
# or from a user's global gitignore.
.DS_Store
